WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.870
Night after night, a weaver
counts his gold into neat squares.

2
00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:06.920
They are his only company.

3
00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:10.740
He loves "their bright faces,
which were all his own".

4
00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:13.880
Then one night, the gold is gone.

5
00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:16.950
Just an empty hole under the floor bricks.

6
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:21.870
Weeks later, by a dying fire, "it seemed
as if there were gold on the floor in

7
00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:23.510
front of the hearth".

8
00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:25.950
Why make him see gold there?

9
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.920
In this mission, you'll work out
what the gold means to Silas.

10
00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:32.260
You'll read the hearth
scene in chapter 12,

11
00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:34.670
and follow the gold to the end.

12
00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:39.640
Your mission: explain why Eliot
makes the curls and the gold alike.
